{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Come on in. Umm, this yoke is frozen again. Right, what brings you in?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): I'm grand, doctor. She dragged me down. I only want to know if I can keep driving, the licence.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Niamh, his sister. I wouldn't have him here only I saw something last month.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): And the chemist had me at one thirty over eighty last week, so it's not the pressure. Sure I'm fine.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, the driving, say that again. I was in the wrong chart.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Driving. No seizure in two years. I drive the van for the deliveries and I want to keep the licence. It's nothing.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): Err, epilepsy still, and you're on the levetiracetam?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah, about six years now. levetirasetam, five hundred milligrams morning and night, by mouth. I don't miss a dose.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He doesn't take the tablets on Sundays.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Ah no. It was the Saturday we were in Killarney, I forgot the morning one. Not Sundays. I'm taking them grand since we got home.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Saturday, so. I still think you missed more than the one.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): One tablet. You're making a whole thing of it.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): Mm. And this thing you saw, Niamh? The screen's after jumping, go on.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Last month, telly on, he went blank. Staring, wouldn't answer me, about a minute, then he was grand like nothing happened.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): That wasn't a seizure. I was uh thinking about the match. I've had none in two years, I told you.",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (DOCTOR): When last month? Sorry, the date, say it again.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Umm, I couldn't tell you the day. Sometime last month. I haven't a clue.",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (DOCTOR): With that, any tongue biting, or did you wet yourself?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Never.",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (DOCTOR): Headache after it?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (DOCTOR): Chest pain?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really. Never.",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (DOCTOR): Asthma's on the old notes. Is that still going?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah, since I was a teenager. Just the blue inhaler, not a bother.",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any wheeze with it?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): No... well, sometimes, if I'm after a run. Two puffs of salbutamol when I need it.",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (DOCTOR): A cough, or tightness in the chest?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): Not that either.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (DOCTOR): Hold on, the inhaler. Two puffs, say it again, I typed the wrong box.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): Two puffs of salbutamol, as I need them. That's the lot.",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He cut his hand in Killarney as well. It healed in five days.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): Did that heal slow, or was there any oozing?",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No. Five days and it was closed, normal.",
  "[SEG0035] person_4 (NURSE): Doctor, he told me one thirty over eighty from the chemist. I've just redone it, 134 over 82, pulse 74, sats 98 percent.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (DOCTOR): Grand. Any fever, or off your food?",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Eating away fine.",
  "[SEG0038] person_1 (DOCTOR): Waterworks or the bowels, any trouble?",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): Not at all.",
  "[SEG0040] person_1 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke, or take a drink?",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (PATIENT): Never smoked. A few pints of a Friday. I live on my own.",
  "[SEG0042] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any operations?",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (PATIENT): No, never under the knife.",
  "[SEG0044] person_1 (DOCTOR): Anyone in the family with seizures?",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (PATIENT): My uncle had fits. That's all.",
  "[SEG0046] person_1 (DOCTOR): Allergies to medicines, or anything else?",
  "[SEG0047] person_2 (PATIENT): No. None.",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (PATIENT): Oh, uh, they did a keppra level a while back. They said it was borderline. I haven't the number.",
  "[SEG0049] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll have a quick listen. Chest is clear, no wheeze just now, and the heart sounds are fine.",
  "[SEG0050] person_1 (DOCTOR): I can't call that minute a definite seizure. It might have been a brief focal seizure, or you zoning out. I can't rule either one out.",
  "[SEG0051] person_1 (DOCTOR): We'll book a blood test today for the levetiracetam level. We might do an eeg if there's another blank spell.",
  "[SEG0052] person_1 (DOCTOR): Until that's clearer, don't drive the van. If it was a seizure you'll have to tell the ndls. And don't be skipping the tablets on a weekend away.",
  "[SEG0053] person_1 (DOCTOR): Come back in three weeks and we'll go through the level.",
  "[SEG0054] person_2 (PATIENT): Three weeks, yeah, if I must. Still think ye are making a big deal of nothing."
 ],
